{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1447264-v20-c20-can-vicissitude-affect-changeling-flesh-also-banality-of-tzimisce","id":1447264,"title":"[V20/C20] Can Vicissitude affect changeling flesh?Also Banality of Tzimisce","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-05-03T14:02:14-07:00","id":1447264,"title":"[V20/C20] Can Vicissitude affect changeling flesh?Also Banality of Tzimisce","content":"So,For those don't play CtD. The changeliings of the game have a true form,disguised between a layer of illusion. For those who play btoh games,in a possible crossover, would a Tzimisce be able to twist the flesh of a Changeling?<br /> Also,do you think a Tzimisce might be less Banal than other Clans? After all,Banality is a force of anti-creativity of sameness and of boredom. Tzimiscer and nothing if not creative,they're ofen creative in evil ways,but creative nonetheless. Could some of them be non banal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T14:16:52-07:00","id":1447267,"title":"","content":"Naturally a Tzimisce could use their discipline to alter the flesh of the changeling\u2019s autumn (mundane, physical) form, I would rule that, even a hypothetical enchanted Tzimisce (enchantment is a process which allows non Changelings to perceive and interact with Changeling/Chimerical reality) could not warp the chimerical flesh. Most of the time the chimerical flesh is not manifest in a way that a Tzimisce could even perceive but even if a Changeling Invoked the Wyrd to make their chimerical selves \u2018real\u2019 within the autumn world I\u2019d still argue that the Changeling\u2019s bodies operate under a different paradigm then Viccissitude. <br /> <br /> But that\u2019s just my idea as a flat crossover ruling. If you\u2019re playing a vampire game with Changeling elements and you want to create a threeheaded Satyr and your group is having fun with it, then a blessing on your house.<br /> <br /> To your questions about Tzimisce banality; I\u2019d agree they\u2019re certainly creative but I\u2019d say that would make them a wellspring of Dark Glamour as well as the banality which they gather as part of their vampiric nature (even if as younger kindred they produce less banality then elders might). While a Changeling might have more of a problem with Dark Glamour then banality with an experimenting Tzimisce, they\u2019re still not gonna have a good time, especially if the Tzimisce is on a Paths of Enlightenment and are thus even further from the very-human Dreams kithain (dream Changelings) are derived from and much closer to the primeval nightmares of the Fomorians or Elder Dark. Which the thallain (nightmare changelings) might celebrate and enjoy but would still be a major problem for most Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T14:21:13-07:00","id":1447268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b